data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 11 / EF Core 11, the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. All synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`) and `SaveChanges()` now throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime — there is no configuration to re-enable them.

### Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

### Why

The Cosmos DB SDK is async-only. The sync-over-async bridge was always a compatibility shim that risked deadlocks and thread-pool starvation. EF Core 11 removes it to eliminate these hazards.

### Migration checklist

1. Replace all sync LINQ terminal operators with `*Async` equivalents
2. Propagate `async/await` up through callers (controllers, services)
3. Replace `SaveChanges()` → `SaveChangesAsync()`
4. Remove the now-obsolete sync-over-async opt-in from your `DbContextOptionsBuilder`
